  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Habitat Day 2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of World Habitat Day is to reflect on the state of our towns and cities. World Habitat Day was established in 1985 by the United Nations General Assembly through Resolution 40/202, and was first celebrated in 1986. The theme for this year&#x2019;s World Habitat Day is Accelerating urban action for a carbon-free world. The Communication Section arranges the Global Observance every year and this year it has teamed up with the Government of Cameroon to arrange a high level morning ceremony and four afternoon roundtables. The main accomplishment is to raise global, regional and national awareness around urban carbon mitigation issues</narrative>
  </description>
